    "description": "Natural Amethyst Crystal Cluster\nGeode Specimen on Display Stand\nAmethyst Quartz & Wood Base, 6 x 6 Inches\nThis natural amethyst geode specimen features a cavity of well-formed purple quartz crystal terminations set against its natural rock matrix. Mounted on a fitted beveled wooden display base with a deep mahogany finish, this piece highlights the contrast between the rough natural exterior and the crystalline interior. Amethyst has long been valued both as an ornamental mineral specimen and for decorative display.\nFeatures a natural cluster of deep purple to lavender amethyst crystal points\nNatural raw rock matrix backing securely mounted to wooden plinth\nBeveled wooden display base with rich dark gloss finish\nMeasures approximately 6 inches in height by 6 inches in width\nCondition:\nThe crystal points are well-preserved with natural growth features, inclusions, and varying tip terminations typical of geological specimens. Natural rough rock matrix on the reverse is solid and stable. The wooden base is structurally sound and stands level with light surface wear, minor edge marks, and handwritten inventory numbers on the unfinished underside.\nThank you for all of your support!",
